title: 'Migrate `pallet-election-provider-multi-block` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-election-provider-multi-block` no longer uses the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait and
    the `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of `submit_unsigned` moved to a
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callback.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callback accepts only `TransactionSource::Local` and
    `TransactionSource::InBlock`, it runs the same checks, and it builds the same transaction
    validity as before.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `Config` supertrait changed from
    `CreateBare<Call<Self>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<Self>>`, and the runtime must put
    `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline.

    The `WeightInfo` trait renamed `validate_unsigned` to `authorize_submit_unsigned`.

crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
